# PUSU live cron — DONCHIAN-ONLY (2026-06-16). Apply on VM: crontab dag/crontab (verify: crontab -l)
# All other streams retired (UI + DB + live): MAIN(:01), IMPULSE(:02), halftp_monitor(*/5)
# removed — see sync/donchian/RETIRED_STREAMS_REPORT.md.
#
# Emit ONLY at the BAR CLOSE (+10s) — no more */10 re-scan. The 1h stream runs on the hour (:00),
# the 30m streams on :00/:30. The signal forms at the bar close so a boundary run catches it; the
# +10s lets Binance finalise the just-closed bar. The emitter writes the RAW setup (Donchian break
# + 4h-dir confirm) and Telegram-alerts it AT FORMATION — NO +0.5R gate here. The +0.5R confirmation
# is DOWNSTREAM: the UI/live module on live data + the nightly backtest on 1m history (prune_live
# drops the failed ones) — so there's nothing to re-check mid-period. The 1.5h lookback re-catches a
# bar if a run is late/missed; canli.py dedups on (symbol, signal_time, direction, mode).
#
# DONCHIAN 1h live emit — on the HOUR (:00:10): Donchian(55) 1h breakout, ER>=0.35 gate
#   (mode='donchian'). Telegram alert at formation.
0 * * * * sleep 10 && cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/canli.py --emit >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# DONCHIAN 30m+4h HYBRID live emit — on :00/:30 (+10s): 30m breakout confirmed by 4h trend
#   (mode='dch30_4h'). Best stream overall (+1106R / 2024-26).
0,30 * * * * sleep 10 && cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/canli.py --emit --tf 30m --confirm-htf 4h >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# DONCHIAN 30m+4h · 6R live emit — on :00/:30 (+10s): same hybrid signals, wider 6R target
#   (mode='dch30_4h6'). MFE-validated: ~2x R/trade vs 4R, OOS-robust across 2024-26.
0,30 * * * * sleep 10 && cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/canli.py --emit --tf 30m --confirm-htf 4h --rr 6 >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# CRON HEALTH-CHECK — Telegram "I'm alive" every 6h (00/06/12/18 UTC) with per-strategy status
#   (last signal + 24h count) + how long ago the emit last scanned. So a quiet, no-signal stretch
#   is never mistaken for a dead cron.
0 */6 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/donchian/heartbeat.py >> $HOME/ict-donchian.log 2>&1
# Daily resolve -> the REALISTIC ·0.5R UI versions (the only ones the UI shows). The non-
#   conservative twins (donchian/dch30_4h/dch30_4h6/d30_4h_so) were removed from the UI, so they
#   are no longer resolved. DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 shifts the entry to the +0.5R confirm level and
#   auto-tags rows with a 'c' suffix; DCH_SO_RUNNER_CAP picks the scale-out runner cap.
# 00:30 — full-TP donchianc / dch30_4hc / dch30_4h6c  +  scale-out d30_4h_soc (cap=4, default).
#         Also self-heals the live table (prune_live drops signals that failed dir-confirm).
30 0 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/sync_daily.py --stream all >> $HOME/ict-sync.log 2>&1
# 00:45 — scale-out 6R cap (same dch30_4h signals, wider runner) -> d30so6c.
45 0 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 DCH_SO_RUNNER_CAP=6 $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/sync_daily.py --stream d30_4h_so >> $HOME/ict-sync.log 2>&1
# 01:00 — scale-out 8R cap -> d30so8c.
0 1 * * * cd $HOME/ict-trade && DCH_ENTRY_AT_CONFIRM=1 DCH_SO_RUNNER_CAP=8 $HOME/ict-trade/.venv/bin/python sync/sync_daily.py --stream d30_4h_so >> $HOME/ict-sync.log 2>&1
